from pathlib import Path
text='''\n\n## November 1 — stable singing reference and Country Roads comparison\nUser reopened singing quality/voice consistency work, naming Country Roads. Audit found the October 26 preferred #2 comparison used default-r2.wav, but future Create Cover and Cover Builder still defaulted to the older, previously converted singing.wav sample.\n\nCreated singing-stable-v1.wav as a byte-identical, separate copy of the preferred default-r2.wav, with SHA-256 provenance in singing-stable-v1.json. SINGING_REFERENCE now points at that versioned file. Chat references, old singing.wav and saved songs are unchanged. Create Cover labels the stable choice; song details identify stable/earlier/custom references. Disabling the stable option still explicitly uses the current chat reference.\n\nCover result metadata now records reference content hash, conversion seed, steps, guidance, smoothing and pitch shift. Requests without a seed use 42; native production already supplied 42. Configured Numba cache under workspace data/music-cache/numba to avoid the observed environment-cache temporary-file stall.\n\nOne controlled 12-second Country Roads audition (36–48s) compares the accepted chat-reference 50-step sample with 70 steps. Same guide/reference content/seed/guidance/key. No extraction/full-song regeneration and no automatic pitch shift. Candidate is an audition, not listening-approved, and production quality remains 50 steps. See exports/singing/country-roads-consistency-20261101. Voice identity cannot be validated from pitch/RMS numbers; user listening remains necessary.\n'''
for f in ['docs/MUSIC_STUDIO.md','docs/DEVLOG.md','docs/NEXT_CHAT_HANDOFF.md']:
 p=Path(f);p.write_text(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')+text,encoding='utf-8')
